module

/-!
Circuit-grouping data for the IxVM kernel toplevel, applied wherever the
kernel is compiled for proving or verifying (see
`CompiledToplevel.groupFunctions`). Empty = no grouping: every constrained
function keeps its singleton circuit. Fill from measured workload
statistics; a stale grouping stays sound (grouping never affects
semantics), only less efficient.
-/

public section

namespace IxVM

-- 15 width bands over the 669 circuits with <0.5% max FFT share across the
-- Nat.add_comm / String.split / Array.extract_append workloads (band split at
-- 1.5x the width floor or 48 members; see cold-groups/cold-grouping-report.md).
-- Function circuits 710 -> 56 (total 730 -> 76). The workload FFT proxy pays
-- ~20-27% for this; the win is everything per-circuit: vk size, commitments,
-- opening points, and the recursive verifier.
